    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37981" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-sŏlĭdus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very solid</i> (late Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, Coripp. Laud. <i><span class="en">Just. 3,
			291</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>very firm</i>, <i>very constant</i>, or <i>steadfast</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praesolidum Simonem dignum cognomine Petri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juvenc. 1, 436</span></i>
			.</div>
